\section{Keep the Pending Updates Separate}

The following sketch models only the two interesting phases for the register assignments; it is not a complete simulator scheduler. At the second rising edge \texttt{first} starts at \(1\), \texttt{second} starts at \texttt{x}, and \(d=0\).

\begin{verbatim}
at t = 10 ns, service the rising edge:
    pending[first]  = d       # sample 0 now
    pending[second] = first   # sample OLD first = 1
    active observer sees (1, X)
apply pending writes during NBA
postponed observer sees (0, 1) # same t, different region
\end{verbatim}

\Cref{fig:visual-307} contrasts the observations at both rising edges. The first transfer leaves \texttt{second} unknown because the design does not reset its state.

