If both assignments in the DUT instead used blocking \verb|=| in that order, the second right-hand side would read the newly assigned \texttt{first}: the intended stage would disappear from the functional model. Splitting blocking assignments across concurrent clocked processes can also create simulator order dependence. Nonblocking assignment protects this old-state transfer; it does not resolve multiple processes writing one register or a testbench changing sampled data on the same edge.
